# Carrier-BSP env consumed by stone-provision-tegraflash.sh.
#
# Seeed reComputer Mini J5012 on JetPack 7.2 (L4T R39.2.0): J501 carrier +
# Jetson AGX Orin 64GB module (P3701-0005). The values below come from Seeed's
# recomputer-mini-agx-orin-j501x.conf (Seeed-Studio/Linux_for_Tegra,
# branch r39.2.0, commit df17ed28201645fcaeb6c8e6fb82a0b4592faefb, sha256
# 40b47214a673746b723aa044a04f4067606755c5bf88fd1db6fdceb1bfa61f7e),
# the conf Seeed's flash.sh selects for this product, except the MB2 file
# (authored in this extension) and the two CHECK pins (also present in the
# stock flashvars). Flash profile is the `jetson-agx-orin` machine, whose
# machine config already bakes TEGRA_BOARDSKU 0005, which the flashvars
# CHECK_BOARDSKU takes. Line numbers below refer to the r39.2.0 conf; the
# values are the same as in its r36.5.0 predecessor, which carries an
# earlier copy of this file under bsp/recomputer-mini-j5012.
#
# Generic knob shape:
#   CARRIER_FV_<NAME>=value   -> patches <NAME> in flashvars
#   CARRIER_ENV_<NAME>=value  -> patches <NAME> in .env.initrd-flash
# See meta-avocado-nvidia/docs/adding-a-jetson-carrier.md.

CARRIER_LABEL="Seeed reComputer Mini J5012 (J501 carrier + Jetson AGX Orin 64GB, P3701-0005)"

# Kernel DTB - conf line, inside update_flash_args_p3737_0000_p3701_0000
# (board_sku 0005 branch, conf lines 90-93):
#   DTB_FILE=tegra234-j501x-0000+p3701-0005-recomputer-mini.dtb;
#
# No CARRIER_FV_TBCDTB_FILE on purpose. The conf sets
# TBCDTB_FILE="${DTB_FILE}" (conf line 99), but the stock flashvars key
# TBCDTB_FILE holds the placeholder "@DTBFILE@" (meta-tegra
# TEGRA_FLASHVAR_TBCDTB_FILE ?= "@DTBFILE@" in tegra-common.inc), not a
# literal, and the initrd-flash env carries DTBFILE. The 2026 feed's
# tegra234-flash-helper.sh (meta-avocado wrynose branch, under
# meta-avocado-nvidia/recipes-bsp/tegra-binaries/tegra-helper-scripts/) takes
# the dtb argument ($2, line 161) and resolves the placeholder to it
# (line 609). Setting DTBFILE here therefore carries the same DTB into
# TBCDTB_FILE at flash time; a literal override would drop the placeholder
# mechanism.
CARRIER_ENV_DTBFILE="tegra234-j501x-0000+p3701-0005-recomputer-mini.dtb"

# Pinmux - conf line 110: PINMUX_CONFIG="recomputer-mini-agx-orin-j501x-pinmux.dtsi";
CARRIER_FV_PINMUX_CONFIG="recomputer-mini-agx-orin-j501x-pinmux.dtsi"

# Pad voltage - conf line 111:
#   PMC_CONFIG="recomputer-mini-agx-orin-j501x-padvoltage-default.dtsi";
CARRIER_FV_PMC_CONFIG="recomputer-mini-agx-orin-j501x-padvoltage-default.dtsi"

# Display engine configuration - conf lines 114-115:
#   OVERLAY_DTB_FILE="L4TConfiguration.dtbo,tegra234-carveouts.dtbo,tegra-optee.dtbo,tegra234-dcb-p3701-0000-hdmi.dtbo";
#   DCE_OVERLAY_DTB_FILE="tegra234-dcb-p3701-0000-hdmi.dtbo";
# The overlay carries the display configuration binary for this carrier's HDMI output,
# which sits on the module's DP2 pins (Mini J501 schematic, HDMI sheet). NVIDIA's stock
# p3701.conf.common sets no DCE overlay, so without this knob the DCE firmware is flashed
# with no HDMI configuration for this carrier. The flashvars key is DCE_OVERLAY. It needs
# the meta-avocado change that always writes that line, because a carrier knob can only
# rewrite a line that already exists, and tegra234-dcb-p3701-0000-hdmi.dtbo has to be
# built and present at flash time (the 2026/next feed publishes only the p3767 overlay).
# Not verified on a board: whether it changes the DCE abort seen on a board running
# 36.4.4 firmware.
CARRIER_FV_DCE_OVERLAY="tegra234-dcb-p3701-0000-hdmi.dtbo"

# UPHY lane and 10G configuration - conf line 109:
#   ODMDATA="gbe-uphy-config-22,nvhs-uphy-config-0,hsio-uphy-config-0,gbe0-enable-10g,hsstp-lane-map-3";
# The stock AGX Orin value (meta-tegra agx-orin.inc, TEGRA_FLASHVAR_ODMDATA) is
#   "gbe-uphy-config-22,hsstp-lane-map-3,nvhs-uphy-config-0,hsio-uphy-config-0,gbe0-enable-10g"
# Compared token by token, the Mini adds nothing: the five tokens are the
# same, including hsio-uphy-config-0, and only the order differs. The full
# Seeed string is kept as is.
# The 2026 line renamed the BitBake variable that bakes the default
# (ODMDATA -> TEGRA_FLASHVAR_ODMDATA in meta-tegra). The carrier knob below
# does not follow that rename, because a CARRIER_ENV_ knob names the key
# inside .env.initrd-flash, and that key is still ODMDATA on the 2026 line:
# tegraflash-bsp.bb writes `ODMDATA="${ODMDATA}"` into .env.initrd-flash and
# tegra234-flash-helper.sh (lines 183-210) reads CARRIER_ENV_ODMDATA's result
# from the environment ahead of the flashvars default. Renaming the knob to
# CARRIER_ENV_TEGRA_FLASHVAR_ODMDATA would target a key that file does not
# have; the parser skips an unknown target with a warning and the knob would
# become dead, leaving the stock string in force (same tokens today, so no
# behaviour change now, but any future carrier-specific token would be lost).
CARRIER_ENV_ODMDATA="gbe-uphy-config-22,nvhs-uphy-config-0,hsio-uphy-config-0,gbe0-enable-10g,hsstp-lane-map-3"

# MB2 BCT misc DTS - the stock flashvars value is
# tegra234-mb2-bct-misc-p3701-0000.dts. The conf has no
# line for it; this file is authored in this extension from the stock
# NVIDIA misc DTS plus the single carrier-EEPROM change Seeed makes (see its
# header). The flashvars key is MB2BCT_CFG, not MB2_BCT (the shell variable
# in p3701.conf.common is renamed on export); patching MB2_BCT would be a
# silent no-op. The authored file is carried over unchanged from the
# R36.5.2 extension and was not re-diffed against the R39.2.0 stock file.
CARRIER_FV_MB2BCT_CFG="tegra234-mb2-bct-misc-p3701-0000-seeed.dts"

# EEPROM comparison - conf lines 86-97: the update_flash_args_p3737_0000_p3701_0000
# board_sku 0005 branch (lines 90-93) is the module this product ships;
# 0004 selects the 32GB DTB and is not this product. The jetson-agx-orin
# machine already bakes TEGRA_BOARDSKU 0005, which meta-tegra's
# TEGRA_FLASH_CHECK_BOARDSKU takes, so these two lines
# are redundant pins; they stay so a 32GB SKU 0004 module fails signing
# even if the machine default moves.
CARRIER_FV_CHECK_BOARDID="3701"
CARRIER_FV_CHECK_BOARDSKU="0005"

# Deliberately not overridden:
#   - SCR_CONFIG: the conf never sets it, so Seeed's flash for the Mini
#     applies the stock SCR file; the stock config is used unchanged.
#   - PMIC / BPMP / SDRAM: the conf's PMIC lines (88, 92) name the stock
#     tegra234-mb1-bct-pmic-p3701-0005.dts, and MIC-733-AO6A1 boots the
#     same SKU-0005 module on the same target with none of these overridden.
